MEX FILE COMPILATION FOR LINUX
(worked on Ubuntu 16.04LTS and Matlab R2017b)



SOME PRELIMINARY INFORMATION

1) the mexopts.sh is not read during compilation. The idea is to replace matlab original mexopts.sh, which can be found in matlab_root_folder/bin. In matlab, type 

matlabroot

to find it your root folder. On my computer, the mexopts.sh file is in

/usr/local/MATLAB/R2017b/bin

2) In Matlab R2017b, there is an other (additionnal) mex option file mex_C_glnxa64.xml in the folder ~/.matlab/R2017b. This file is usefull to link Matlab to a given gcc version, if several gcc versions are installed on the computer. Just change the "Location" line to point to the gcc versoin that matlab wants. In my case, I have change to line to 

Location="/usr/bin/gcc-4.9"

3) I have not been able to correctly used the mex option file, and thus put all the information in the Makefile.

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

COMPILATION OF THE FORTRAN

1) open the Makefile, comments the lines associated to the sunstudio compiler (lines 12-15), and uncomment the lines associated to gfortran (lines 20-21)

2) In the variable FFLAGS
--> add -cpp 
--> replace -M $(MODDIR) by -I $(MODDIR)

3) After this try to compile. There will be a bug. However, the fortran compilation should work, and the bug occurs only in the mex compilation. The error is 

mkrak.c:(.text+0x27f): undefined reference to `kraken_'


%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

MEX COMPILATION

The mess compilation crashes because there is an issue between the fortran and the c codes. This is probably due to the mexopts.sh that is not properly used. One way around this is to replace the Makefile line

	mex mkrak.c 

by 

	mex -L"/usr/bin/" mkrak.c obj/zsecx.o	obj/zbrentx.o obj/bcimp.o obj/kuping.o obj/sinvitd.o obj/mergev.o obj/weight.o obj/twersk.o obj/subtab.o obj/readin.o obj/errout.o obj/sorti.o obj/splinec.o obj/krakmod.o obj/sdrdrmod.o obj/kraken.o -lgfortran

Note that in this line
--> "/usr/bin/" is the folder where your gcc is installed.

